{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"prompt\": \"Minecraft builder reference sheet, landscape approximately 3:2, crisp vanilla Minecraft voxel style, plain light background, no characters or animals. Two views side by side at the same block scale: LEFT straight-on orthographic front elevation; RIGHT elevated three-quarter view from the street showing the whole 36-block-wide x 48-block-deep Roman domus and its open courts. Skilled human builder quality: real massing, projecting cornices and pilasters, recessed framed openings, real roof verges, eaves and ridge, stairs/slabs/fences/walls/trapdoors/lantern details. Single storey, walls to y6, ridges to y9, symmetrical centre axis.\\nStreet facade: long cream plaster wall on stone-brick plinth, lower two courses red-painted dado, cut-sandstone cornice. Low red-tile gable roof with brick-red and granite tiles, mud-brick eave, pale quartz ridge. Exactly four open shop windows with masonry counters, decorated clay pots and spruce shutters folded flat on both sides, two windows each side of centre. Four-wide recessed central entrance passage (fauces), two white marble pilasters and three-step white pediment. Two double spruce doors set back inside, fanlight above formed with copper_bars, stone sidewalk step, bronze lampstands and potted ferns beside entry.\\nBehind front block, roofs fall inward toward bright atrium with black-and-white checker mosaic, open sky through 8x6 block opening. Four dark-oak Tuscan columns at corners, shallow rain pool impluvium with white marble coping below, four small red-tile roof strips sloping inward. On axis tablinum study through white pilasters leads to peristyle: exactly 18 white marble columns with chiseled capitals, continuous white architrave, red-tile sheds sloping inward. Garden: two symmetrical parterre beds with clipped azalea hedges, red and blue flowers, white marble fountain basin with central pedestal and water bowls, abstract block-built white statues on stone plinths (decorative sculptures only, no living people), rose bushes, potted plants, bronze lanterns hanging between columns. Small barred windows, triclinium with three red couches made from red_bed/red_carpet, cubicula, kitchen hearth and tall brick chimney on WEST (left from street), rear service door close the block. Interiors may be naturally occluded by roofs; keep exterior and courtyards coherent.\\nUse ONLY these exact vanilla block ids, named in a compact readable palette key beneath the views grouped by role; use shape variants as named:\\nplaster: smooth_sandstone, end_stone_bricks, sandstone, smooth_sandstone_stairs, smooth_sandstone_slab.\\ndado: red_terracotta.\\nplinth: stone_bricks, stone_brick_stairs, stone_brick_slab, stone_brick_wall, chiseled_stone_bricks.\\ncornice: cut_sandstone, cut_sandstone_slab.\\nmarble: quartz_block, smooth_quartz, quartz_pillar, chiseled_quartz_block, quartz_stairs, quartz_slab, smooth_quartz_slab, smooth_quartz_stairs, diorite_wall, polished_diorite.\\nroof: bricks, granite, polished_granite, mangrove_planks, mud_bricks, brick_stairs, brick_slab, granite_stairs, granite_slab, polished_granite_stairs, polished_granite_slab, mangrove_stairs, mangrove_slab, mud_brick_stairs, mud_brick_slab.\\ntimber: spruce_planks, spruce_slab, spruce_stairs, spruce_trapdoor, spruce_door, spruce_fence, dark_oak_planks, dark_oak_log, dark_oak_slab, dark_oak_stairs, dark_oak_fence, dark_oak_trapdoor, dark_oak_door.\\nbronze: copper_lantern, copper_chain, copper_bars, copper_block, cut_copper, cut_copper_slab, cut_copper_stairs, copper_trapdoor.\\nmosaic: quartz_block, polished_blackstone, red_terracotta, black_terracotta, white_terracotta, yellow_terracotta, blue_terracotta, terracotta, orange_terracotta, cyan_glazed_terracotta, blue_glazed_terracotta, orange_glazed_terracotta, smooth_stone, polished_andesite.\\nground: grass_block, dirt, gravel, dirt_path, andesite, polished_andesite, coarse_dirt, podzol.\\np